.TH AMERIKA-LOGIN 1 "2026-10-21" "Amerika OS" "Amerika OS Manual"
.SH NAME
amerika\-login \- switch the Amerika OS login screen on or off
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amerika\-login
.RB { status | enable | disable | preview }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B amerika\-login
controls the retro\-futurist SDDM login theme installed by the
.B amerika\-login
package. Installing the package changes nothing; the login screen is used only after
.B amerika\-login enable
and only from the next start of the computer. The current session is never stopped or restarted.
.PP
.B enable
and
.B disable
ask for administrator rights through
.BR pkexec (1)
and run
.IR /usr/libexec/amerika/amerika\-login\-helper .
Enabling remembers the previous display manager; disabling returns to it.
If SDDM fails to start three times within 90 seconds, the helper switches back to the previous
display manager on its own (the unit
.IR amerika\-login\-fallback.service ).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print the current display manager, whether the Amerika login screen is active, and the remembered previous manager, as JSON.
.TP
.B enable
Use SDDM with the Amerika theme from the next start.
.TP
.B disable
Go back to the previous display manager from the next start.
.TP
.B preview
Show the greeter in a test window for 30 seconds (needs a running graphical session).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/sddm/themes/amerika
The theme.
.TP
.I /etc/sddm.conf.d/50\-amerika.conf
Written by
.BR enable ,
removed by
.BR disable .
.TP
.I /var/lib/amerika\-os/login/previous.json
The display manager to return to.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 for a usage error or missing privileges.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR amerika\-boot (1),
.BR amerika\-flavour (7),
.BR sddm (1)
